From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd: release the tx wakelock when the last packet completes

dhd_prot_txdata() takes wlan_txfl_wake for MAX_TX_TIMEOUT (500 ms) on
every queued packet, and nothing ever calls dhd_txfl_wake_unlock(): each
transmit keeps the AP awake for the full timeout even though the dongle
reports completion within milliseconds. With the screen off the y2slte
recorded 1179 wlan_txfl_wake wakeups and 1078 s held in about 1.5 h.

Drop the wakelock in dhd_prot_txstatus_process() once active_tx_count
reaches zero. The timeout is kept as a safety net for lost completions;
if a completion races ahead of the counter increment the old behavior
(timeout only) applies.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd_msgbuf.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd_msgbuf.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd_msgbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd_msgbuf.c
@@ -6503,6 +6503,7 @@
 	void *dmah;
 	void *secdma;
 	bool pkt_fate;
+	int tx_pending;
 	msgbuf_ring_t *ring = &dhd->prot->d2hring_tx_cpln;
 #if defined(TX_STATUS_LATENCY_STATS)
 	flow_info_t *flow_info;
@@ -6555,8 +6556,17 @@
 #endif
 
 	DHD_INFO(("txstatus for pktid 0x%04x\n", pktid));
-	if (OSL_ATOMIC_DEC_RETURN(dhd->osh, &prot->active_tx_count) < 0) {
+	tx_pending = OSL_ATOMIC_DEC_RETURN(dhd->osh, &prot->active_tx_count);
+	if (tx_pending < 0) {
 		DHD_ERROR(("Extra packets are freed\n"));
+	} else if (tx_pending == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * The last queued packet has completed, so the host has nothing
+		 * left to wait for: drop the tx wakelock now instead of letting
+		 * MAX_TX_TIMEOUT expire. The timeout stays as a safety net for
+		 * lost completions.
+		 */
+		DHD_TXFL_WAKE_UNLOCK(dhd);
 	}
 	ASSERT(pktid != 0);
 
